{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat","id":1008677,"title":"Viking Werewolves and Mass Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T14:09:59-08:00","id":1008677,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Viking Werewolves and Mass Combat","content":"Hi!<br /> I'm about to run a Werewolf campaign with The Wolf and the Raven from the Chronicles of Darkness: Dark Eras.<br /> Now, I'm sure this came up on another thread, but what about systems for raiding? I'm not talking about large armies, these are 20 x 20 people battles, max. A bunch of family members versus a bunch of housecarls.<br /> I thought on using the Down and Dirty combat rules, but I think it might be a bit anticlimactic. I also thought on using something like that training tactic in Hunter, where one character is the secondary actor for a bunch of primary actors; in this case, the commander and the raiding party, but I figured it wouldn't quite work.<br /> Any thoughts or ideas?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, should I use the farming rules from Mirrors? Or is it better to leave that to storytelling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T14:18:27-08:00","id":1008680,"title":"","content":"Have you considered using the Brief Nightmares rules from the Horrors section of the core book? Just treat each group as a single Nightmare with a collective &quot;Best At,&quot; &quot;Worst At,&quot; and &quot;All Other&quot; dice pool, a shared Aspiration. Dread Powers can represent distinguishing features like being better armed or armored, or having siege equipment, and Banes can represent weak points in the unit. Larger armies can use the &quot;Lone Terror&quot; stats, mid-sized battalions can use &quot;Horde&quot; stats, and small stands can use &quot;Minion&quot; stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-26-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:37:39-08:00","id":1008698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1008680#post1008680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered using the Brief Nightmares rules from the Horrors section of the core book? Just treat each group as a single Nightmare with a collective &quot;Best At,&quot; &quot;Worst At,&quot; and &quot;All Other&quot; dice pool, a shared Aspiration. Dread Powers can represent distinguishing features like being better armed or armored, or having siege equipment, and Banes can represent weak points in the unit. Larger armies can use the &quot;Lone Terror&quot; stats, mid-sized battalions can use &quot;Horde&quot; stats, and small stands can use &quot;Minion&quot; stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know that existed. Definitively will be looking into it, thanks a bunch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T11:51:10-08:00","id":1008988,"title":"","content":"Here are my own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">Mass Combat rules for <b>CoD</b></a>, inspired by Chase rules and <b>Savage Worlds</b> combat mechanics. They were devised by me because of my own planned Viking <b>Werewolf </b>game.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my modern revision I would only use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> idea, and write each Unit as Brief Nightmare each Important Character can attack on their actions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:02:22-08:00","id":1009100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1008988#post1008988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are my own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">Mass Combat rules for <b>CoD</b></a>, inspired by Chase rules and <b>Savage Worlds</b> combat mechanics. They were devised by me because of my own planned Viking <b>Werewolf </b>game.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my modern revision I would only use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> idea, and write each Unit as Brief Nightmare each Important Character can attack on their actions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty well written! Thanks a bunch, I think this one might fit more the idea I had in mind! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:43:13-08:00","id":1009147,"title":"","content":"one of the wild west books for werewolf the apocalypse had mass combat rules (in the vein of the civil war mind you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:52:18-08:00","id":1009210,"title":"","content":"One thing to take in consideration with my Mass Combat rules on Uratha - they can enter Death Rage. As Battle Action is 15 minutes, it means that character can declare one attack target and it ends - if character insists on running in Gauru or getting 'immortality' ( instant Regeneration ), he goes in Hard Rage, risking massacre on whole his units - depending on Primal Urge, it can even take few Battle Turns. Not to mention he can roll other werewolves in Rage themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T05:50:56-08:00","id":1009291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009147#post1009147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the wild west books for werewolf the apocalypse had mass combat rules (in the vein of the civil war mind you).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know anything about Werewolf the Apocalypse, if I had to adapt I would have to convert it from oWoD to nWoD 1e and then 2e, but it just might give me some ideas!<br /> In any case, thanks for the suggestion!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T05:54:18-08:00","id":1009292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009210#post1009210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to take in consideration with my Mass Combat rules on Uratha - they can enter Death Rage. As Battle Action is 15 minutes, it means that character can declare one attack target and it ends - if character insists on running in Gauru or getting 'immortality' ( instant Regeneration ), he goes in Hard Rage, risking massacre on whole his units - depending on Primal Urge, it can even take few Battle Turns. Not to mention he can roll other werewolves in Rage themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! I can clearly imagine an Uratha leading a unit getting more and more pissed off, until he sees someone of the pack getting hurt. Just his luck. That was his trigger. A giant demonic wolf-thing then erupts from behind the shieldwall and tears apart a whole unit.<br /> Just a curiosity, how would you deal with Lunacy in large battles like these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:40:13-08:00","id":1009305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009292#post1009292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a curiosity, how would you deal with Lunacy in large battles like these?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, use Brief Nightmares rules for each Units - yes, this mean that each ship crew will be one Unit and probably be a Horde as Nightmare Type.<br /> <br /> Second, Lunacy works as Breaking Points for humans. But Integrity Breaking Points are all about Willpower ( Resolve + Composure ) dicepools. So use Nightmares 2 * Willpower per Scene - it will work, more or less as Willpower trait in normal characters spread. As Important Characters combat actions are Down &amp; Dirty Combat, treat their <b>direct</b> ( not Battle ) Successes as penalty to Unit's Willpower roll. Add form modifier. You can take easily +4 bonus for the numbers, as Unit is large crowd to begin from. If Lunacy dicepool is &gt;2, it mostly will get success, so resolve whole Unit as under Conditions - they will probably can live if someone survive. If Lunacy &lt;3, they will get extreme Conditions and surly die all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:42:55-08:00","id":1009308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009305#post1009305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, use Brief Nightmares rules for each Units - yes, this mean that each ship crew will be one Unit and probably be a Horde as Nightmare Type.<br /> <br /> Second, Lunacy works as Breaking Points for humans. But Integrity Breaking Points are all about Willpower ( Resolve + Composure ) dicepools. So use Nightmares 2 * Willpower per Scene - it will work, more or less as Willpower trait in normal characters spread. As Important Characters combat actions are Down &amp; Dirty Combat, treat their <b>direct</b> ( not Battle ) Successes as penalty to Unit's Willpower roll. Add form modifier. You can take easily +4 bonus for the numbers, as Unit is large crowd to begin from. If Lunacy dicepool is &gt;2, it mostly will get success, so resolve whole Unit as under Conditions - they will probably can live if someone survive. If Lunacy &lt;3, they will get extreme Conditions and surly die all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a bit catastrophic. Which means I am sure one of my players will try it at some point.<br /> Thanks a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T08:35:52-08:00","id":1009343,"title":"","content":"As I want to make revision of those rules and I will not run them in near future - I will gladly read how your battle running on them went. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:15:06-08:00","id":1009400,"title":"","content":"Err... I wouldn't recommend rolling a Unit's Willpower for a Breaking Point. I would recommend using their Best At dice pool if they are best at resisting Breaking Points, their Worst At dice pool if they're worst at resisting Breaking Points, and their All Other dice pool otherwise. Just like they do for everything else that requires a dice roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:49:40-08:00","id":1009414,"title":"","content":"First off - we do not talk here about <i>literal</i> Breaking Points of Lunacy victims. Units/Brief Nightmares do not have 'mass Integrity', common to each character in group. It's just Lunacy rules are based on Breaking Points, so we analyzing if we can <b>sidestep</b> Integrity trait all together, as we do not have those on Units. Luckily, mortal Breaking Points are, in reality, dicepool of Willpower+Integrity Modifier. We throw away Modifier and have clear Willpower dicepool - enough eyeballing for battle conditions.<br /> <br /> Second - I would not use 'Best Dice Pool / Worst Dice Pool / All Other Pools' for two other reasons - those dicepools are too lower/higher than typical Willpower of proper characters - they are 7/1/3 for Horde ( typical Unit ), which are 'very good/ terrible / lower than average' on comparing to Willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It would mean that any Lunacy roll will be failed or will be almost sure to succeed, nothing in between. And it would mean that one boat of Viking warriors will be much more likely to run from any Uratha threat than one typical Viking ( Willpower 4 ) on his own, which is illogical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, judging if 'Resisting Lunacy' should be Best/Worst/Other dicepool with each Unit is tedious. Assuming standard Willpower, like we assume standardization of other Traits of Unit ( by using Brief Nightmares ), is much more 'storytelling efficient', especially, as we still takes characters actions in considerations by using Forms modifiers or Actions Success as penalties to Lunacy roll, in the end.<br /> <br /> On general, I think that make Unit 'typical' Willpower dicepool and using it most of the time will be much more elegant and less rules cluttered on running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-28-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:24:22-08:00","id":1009427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009414#post1009414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off - we do not talk here about <i>literal</i> Breaking Points of Lunacy victims. Units/Brief Nightmares do not have 'mass Integrity', common to each character in group. It's just Lunacy rules are based on Breaking Points, so we analyzing if we can <b>sidestep</b> Integrity trait all together, as we do not have those on Units. Luckily, mortal Breaking Points are, in reality, dicepool of Willpower+Integrity Modifier. We throw away Modifier and have clear Willpower dicepool - enough eyeballing for battle conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand that we're not talking about literal Integrity Breaking Points here. But as you observed, Integrity Breaking Points use a dice pool, which means Nightmares would use either their Best At, Worst At, or All Other dice pool, like they do for everything else that requires a dice roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009414#post1009414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second - I would not use for two other reasons - 'Best Dice Pool / Worst Dice Pool / All Other Pools' are too lower/higher than typical Willpower of proper characters - they are 7/1/3 for Horde ( typical Unit ), which are 'very good/ terrible / lower than average' on comparing to Willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It would mean that any Lunacy roll will be failed or will be almost sure to succeed, nothing in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, a dice pool of 3 is by no means &quot;almost sure to succeed&quot;. It's about a 66% chance of success, which is pretty good, but with a realistic chance of failure. It's also fewer dice than an average character has on a neutral Breaking Point (which would be 4 to 5). Most Units would probably have resisting Lunacy as &quot;all other&quot;, unless they're specialized werewolf hunters or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009414#post1009414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it would mean that one boat of Viking warriors will be much more likely to run from any threat than one typical Viking ( Willpower 4 ) on his own, which is illogical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not illogical when you remember that Units are abstract representations of groups of people. If the Unit fails its Lunacy roll, it's not literally the whole crew of Vikings collectively succumbing to Lunacy simultaneously. It's the aggregate effect of Lunacy affecting some members of the crew culminating in an overall negative impact on the crew's ability to function as a unit. It makes perfect sense that a single individual Viking has a slightly better chance of resisting Lunacy than an entire crew has of not being affected by Lunacy, simply because the crew has more people. If a few members of the crew start freaking out when they see a werewolf and can't do their job, the whole crew suffers for it, even if the rest of them are fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009414#post1009414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, judging if 'Resisting Lunacy' should be Best/Worst/Other dicepool with each Unit is tedious. Assuming standard Willpower, like we assume standardization of other Traits of Unit ( by using Brief Nightmares ), is much more 'storytelling efficient', especially, as we still takes characters actions in considerations by using Forms modifiers or Actions Success as penalties to Lunacy roll, in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to decide if each Unit should have resisting Lunacy as Best/Worst/Other. It should almost always just be other, unless you specifically want the Unit to be especially good or bad at it. That's the whole point of having those be the categories. By default, everything a Nightmare does will be rolled with their &quot;All Other&quot; dice pool. Then you pick a few things you want them to be specialized in and a few things you want them to struggle with, and those things use their &quot;Best At&quot; and &quot;Worst At&quot; respectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009414#post1009414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I think that make Unit 'typical' Willpower dicepool and using it most of the time will be much more elegant and less rules cluttered on running.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's less elegant and more cluttered. Only having to remember three dice pools, and using either the best, the worst, or the one for everything else is elegant. It's simple. You never have to worry about &quot;what do I roll when such-and-such happens?&quot; You just always use the All Other dice pool unless something fits under their best or worst tasks. The more exceptions you add to that formula, the more specific cases you have to remember and the more complicated you make the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:40:21-08:00","id":1009466,"title":"","content":"As to 'you should not use Willpower Trait' argument - you still use it. Brief Nightmares have Willpower limit per scene you should remember to use, even on Battle. Using this also as Lunacy treshold is just more convinient and accurate in this example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009427#post1009427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes perfect sense that a single individual Viking has a slightly better chance of resisting Lunacy than an entire crew has of not being affected by Lunacy, simply because the crew has more people. If a few members of the crew start freaking out when they see a werewolf and can't do their job, the whole crew suffers for it, even if the rest of them are fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is totally <i>contrary</i> to the spirit of Lunacy rules. Just see this part of text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When groups of witnesses work together, they suffer lessened Lunacy. When two characters are focused on the same task together, each receives a +1 bonus to his breaking point rolls. When a small group (usually around five or less) works together, they each receive +2. Large groups (ten or fewer) gain +3. Any larger mob receives +4.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Groups</i> should be more resistant to Lunacy than individuals. It was heart of Lunacy in Forsaken as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:58:46-08:00","id":1009471,"title":"","content":"One person with 4 dice has a 24.01% chance of failing the Lunacy roll. One person in a crowd with 20 people (8 dice) has roughly a 5.76% chance of failing the Lunacy roll.<br /> However, and that's what I think Charlaquin is referring to, there's roughly a 69,7% chance that at least one person in that group will fail the Lunacy roll just because of the number of people who has to check for it. The bonus helps the individual, but it's not enough to mitigate the increased risk of at least one person failing in larger groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:36:36-08:00","id":1009485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009466#post1009466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to 'you should not use Willpower Trait' argument - you still use it. Brief Nightmares have Willpower limit per scene you should remember to use, even on Battle. Using this also as Lunacy treshold is just more convinient and accurate in this example.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't use it as a dice pool. You use it like normal Willpower - a resource you spend to add dice to dice pools. The dice pools themselves are always either Best At, Worst At, or Other. They can still be modified with bonuses or penalties, such as spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009466#post1009466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is totally <i>contrary</i> to the spirit of Lunacy rules. Just see this part of text:<br /> <br /> <i>Groups</i> should be more resistant to Lunacy than individuals. It was heart of Lunacy in Forsaken as always.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bonus applies to the rolls individuals make. But a Unit isn't an individual, it's an abstraction representing the collective efforts of a group of people. Sure, each individual member of the crew would theoretically have +4 to their Lunacy rolls, but the whole point of abstracting a group into a single unit for the purposes of mass combat is so you don't have to make those rolls individually. You just make a single roll for the whole group. On a success, the aggregate effect of Lunacy on the group is not enough to negatively impact their functionality as a combat unit. On a failure, it is. As Tessie says, even if being in a group makes it easier for the crew members to resist Lunacy, the fact that they are a large group means more opportunities for failure among the crew, and since the crew rely on each other to function as a unit, one or two crew members succumbing can mess it up for everyone else. When your helmsman is having a panic attack, it doesn't really matter that all your oarsmen are fine. Using the &quot;all other&quot; dice pool is just an abstraction, checking to see if the Unit overall is able to cope with the fact that some of its members might be falling to Lunacy or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:52:30-08:00","id":1009725,"title":"","content":"You write like one or two members of Unit being scared of werewolf is all problem. If typical Unit have 10-20 people ( Viking ship, Roman Contubernium ) two people falling to Lunacy are not problem - every soldier is a bit scared when seeing 2,5 meters death machine. If it would be like 30% <i>maybe</i> we can talk about proper effects of Lunacy on Unit at large. More reasonable is like 50% of Unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:19:27-08:00","id":1009845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009725#post1009725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You write like one or two members of Unit being scared of werewolf is all problem. If typical Unit have 10-20 people ( Viking ship, Roman Contubernium ) two people falling to Lunacy are not problem - every soldier is a bit scared when seeing 2,5 meters death machine. If it would be like 30% <i>maybe</i> we can talk about proper effects of Lunacy on Unit at large. More reasonable is like 50% of Unit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of using a Unit as an abstraction of a large number of people is that you're not looking at specific numbers like &quot;three people have been affected by Lunacy&quot; or &quot;10% of the crew&quot;. It's abstract. If you fail the roll, the Lunacy has affected the crew, in aggregate, enough that their functionality as a unit has been compromised. How specifically that happened isn't important, it's abstract. That's what you want in mass combat rules, so you don't need to worry about every single soldier. Just like the Unit taking 1 lethal doesn't mean every single crew member has taken 1 lethal. Maybe one died, or maybe a couple were seriously injured. What happened to the individual crewmen is abstracted in favor of focusing on how close the unit as a whole is to being neutralized as a combatant. Likewise, maybe the Captain is the only one with Lunacy, or maybe 50% of the crew is, it doesn't really matter. What matters is, as a group, their ability overall has been affected by the fact that some of the crew is being affected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:34:47-08:00","id":1009853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1008680#post1008680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered using the Brief Nightmares rules from the Horrors section of the core book? Just treat each group as a single Nightmare with a collective &quot;Best At,&quot; &quot;Worst At,&quot; and &quot;All Other&quot; dice pool, a shared Aspiration. Dread Powers can represent distinguishing features like being better armed or armored, or having siege equipment, and Banes can represent weak points in the unit. Larger armies can use the &quot;Lone Terror&quot; stats, mid-sized battalions can use &quot;Horde&quot; stats, and small stands can use &quot;Minion&quot; stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear I've read the core book damn near cover to cover in the last few weeks. Somehow, I still missed this section, or at least, never thought through the utility of using it for something like this. You are promoted to my favorite person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:34:52-08:00","id":1009854,"title":"","content":"Great, <b>Charl</b>, it's abstract. But saying 'even one of them should fail and whole Unit failed' is not working in this situation. Unit is abstracted, but we must then consider <b>whole</b> of it reaction, not that each one scared soldier is great problem for it. Then, if we look on Unit as about 20 men facing werewolf, higher average Lunacy pool is totally okay. More, it's really logical in this situation. And correct with rules for Lunacy on groups.<br /> <br /> 'All other' is only 3 dices, which is lower than average dicepool of each soldier. Twice of it, or Willpower per scene, is 6 that is nicely higher - and working as <b>group</b>'s Lunacy base dicepool in my POV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:39:14-08:00","id":1009857,"title":"","content":"A large mob only gets a +4 to their check, they're not meant to be immune. Seeing a werewolf in gauru form gives a -2, further modified by Primal Urge. A Primal Urge 10 werewolf in gauru form offers a -7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:47:18-08:00","id":1009861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009857#post1009857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A large mob only gets a +4 to their check, they're not meant to be immune. Seeing a werewolf in gauru form gives a -2, further modified by Primal Urge. A Primal Urge 10 werewolf in gauru form offers a -7.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? With Lunacy base of 6, instead of 3, you only get's +2 bonus beyond avarage one soldier. Like... five or less members Lunacy bonus? It's still a bit less than proper PC would get from this situation, but it's still twice what <b>Charl</b> is proposing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:06:47-08:00","id":1009869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009854#post1009854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, <b>Charl</b>, it's abstract. But saying 'even one of them should fail and whole Unit failed' is not working in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that if one soldier fails the whole Unit fails. I'm saying it doesn't matter what happens to individual soldiers. The Unit rolls as a group, and they fail as a group. If the Unit fails it's roll, enough of the crew is affected by Lunacy that the Unit as a whole is affected. By whatever standard you feel like using for how many of them you think need to be affected for it to count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009854#post1009854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unit is abstracted, but we must then consider <b>whole</b> of it reaction, not that each one scared soldier is great problem for it. Then, if we look on Unit as about 20 men facing werewolf, higher average Lunacy pool is totally okay. More, it's really logical in this situation. And correct with rules for Lunacy on groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no rules for Lunacy on groups. There are rules for Lunacy rolls made by individual characters who are part of a group. We are not making rolls for individual characters who are part of a group, we are making one roll for an abstract combat Unit. And if we are using the Brief Nightmare rules to represent that Unit, then to comply with the Brief Nightmare rules, all of the Units dice pools must be &quot;Best At&quot;, &quot;Worst At&quot;, or all other. You can apply bonuses and/or penalties to those dice pools if you think that makes it more &quot;logical&quot; or whatever, but Nightmares don't roll Willpower as a dice pool. They have exactly three dice pools, pick one and use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009854#post1009854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'All other' is only 3 dices, which is lower than average dicepool of each soldier. Twice of it, or Willpower per scene, is 6 that is nicely higher - and working as <b>group</b>'s Lunacy base dicepool in my POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really matter that the group's dice pool is lower than an individual soldier's dice pool, because we are using a different set of rules for the group than we do for individual characters. Using the &quot;all other&quot; dice pool for a Unit to resist lunacy just means that the group, as a whole, has a roughly 66% chance of not being impacted enough in aggregate by the influence of Lunacy to be worth modeling mechanically. They have a 44% chance that the aggregate effect on the group is enough to warrant putting a Lunacy Condition on the Unit. If those numbers don't feel right to you, give them some situational bonus dice, or make it their Best At. But don't just roll their Willpower as a dice pool, that's not a thing Nightmares can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:12:49-08:00","id":1009870,"title":"","content":"Anyway, the whole &quot;the Unit has a worse dice pool than an individual soldier&quot; argument is pretty pointless since Units and individual characters operate under different rules. Heck, a Minion's Best At pool is 5. That's the same as an average soldier's Weaponry dice pool would be. You don't seem to consider it a problem that a small Unit of troops wouldn't be any more effective at melee combat as a whole than any single member of the group. Why is that any different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:52:36-08:00","id":1009901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009870#post1009870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the whole &quot;the Unit has a worse dice pool than an individual soldier&quot; argument is pretty pointless since Units and individual characters operate under different rules. Heck, a Minion's Best At pool is 5. That's the same as an average soldier's Weaponry dice pool would be. You don't seem to consider it a problem that a small Unit of troops wouldn't be any more effective at melee combat as a whole than any single member of the group. Why is that any different?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>did not</i> written I agree with assessment that Minion Stats are good to represent most Units. I would even point they are <b>not</b> - Minion would be for this lone, not very special individual soldier or vehicle you find sometimes in smaller battles. Most infantry squads and similar would use Horde Stats. Lone Terror would be for those true war machines and their crew - catapults, cannons or early tanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:12:29-08:00","id":1010003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1009725#post1009725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You write like one or two members of Unit being scared of werewolf is all problem. If typical Unit have 10-20 people ( Viking ship, Roman Contubernium ) two people falling to Lunacy are not problem - every soldier is a bit scared when seeing 2,5 meters death machine. If it would be like 30% <i>maybe</i> we can talk about proper effects of Lunacy on Unit at large. More reasonable is like 50% of Unit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is. The old Norse combat style relied heavily on the shield wall. When the shield wall breaks, such as if one of the members is struck by Lunacy, the entire line is damaged by it.<br /> The cohesion of the unit is badly hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:45:06-08:00","id":1010075,"title":"","content":"Okay, so in this take it would mean that any Gauru sighting in battle ends it instantly in mass Lunacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If one soldier is needed to make mass histeria in Unit, the they base dicepool should be like 2, tops 3. Then we add penalties from Form alone and this mean that each battle with werewolves ends in all humans slaughter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i>Without</i> even taking things like morale from fighting enemy ( penalties from Important Characters Down &amp; Dirty ).<br /> <br /> We higher Lunacy dicepool to numbers of 4-6, or this system is without any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-30-2016, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:57:11-08:00","id":1010079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so in this take it would mean that any Gauru sighting in battle ends it instantly in mass Lunacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If one soldier is needed to make mass histeria in Unit, the they base dicepool should be like 2, tops 3. Then we add penalties from Form alone and this mean that each battle with werewolves ends in all humans slaughter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i>Without</i> even taking things like morale from fighting enemy ( penalties from Important Characters Down &amp; Dirty ).<br /> <br /> We higher Lunacy dicepool to numbers of 4-6, or this system is without any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is wrong with that? The unit would either become needlessly aggressive (Atavism), break (Delusion), or become a target for spirits (Reception).<br /> And I think that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:43:26-08:00","id":1010092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010079#post1010079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is wrong with that? The unit would either become needlessly aggressive (Atavism), break (Delusion), or become a target for spirits (Reception).<br /> And I think that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's instant death to any Unit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's like all the werewolves PCs would be in each Battle to just declare 'going Gauru, killing everybody, Battle ended'. In this situation no need for any Battle rules in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When mortals have not any chance to leave confrontation with even starting Gauru, Battle Rules do not have any sense for using them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And all Uratha commanders just say to their mortal packmates 'stend back, I will kill everyone on my own.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:56:44-08:00","id":1010096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010092#post1010092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's instant death to any Unit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's like all the werewolves PCs would be in each Battle to just declare 'going Gauru, killing everybody, Battle ended'. In this situation no need for any Battle rules in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When mortals have not any chance to leave confrontation with even starting Gauru, Battle Rules do not have any sense for using them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And all Uratha commanders just say to their mortal packmates 'stend back, I will kill everyone on my own.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, making the enemy side into raging berserkers is an instant death? Making them more receptive to spirits is?<br /> Yes, making them break will be a victory for the werewolf side, but that is provided all enemy groups break and retreat.<br /> <br /> The Lunacy conditions aren't instant kill stuff, you know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T02:52:41-08:00","id":1010122,"title":"","content":"Let's run some test scenario. Assume we have Viking defending Unit vs Viking attacking Uratha commander. Unit just use stats from Horde Brief Nightmare, Uratha commander have starting 2 dots in any Attributes and Skills needed, Primal Urge 1. So we have this situation then...<br /> <br /> Uratha is attacking Unit. He takes Gauru form. He now has Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4 and Weaponry and Brawl Skills at 2 and do +2 Lethal damage from Tooth or Claws.<br /> <br /> In contrast, out Viking Unit would have: Best Dice Pool 7 ( probably Fighting or Swords &amp; Axes, maybe Shield Defense ), Worst Dice Pool 1 and All Other Pools 3. It has Health of 9 and general Defense as 3. Interesting is this quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p.144</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For resisted actions, use All Other Pools value as resistance Attribute <i>unless</i> Best Dice Pool or Worst Dice Pool actions would be more relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we <b>should</b> use 2*All Other Pools, as Lunacy roll is Resolve + Composure in normal situations.<br /> <br /> Now, to the proper fight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Uratha declares his Attack Battle Action. He assumes Gauru as Instant action and charg\u00e9 on Vikings Unit. He uses his Claws with his Brawl 2 so he get\u2019s Attack Dicepool 7. Unit is defending themselves \u2013 use Shield Defense of 7. Very equal in here. If Unit would use it normal Defense, it would be 7 vs 3 \u2013 much more in favor of Uratha. For ease of test, let\u2019s assume Uratha get only 1 Success more than Unit. It would be then 3 Lethals for Unit, it is 1/3 of starting Health. ( Number of Damage done to Unit is also casualties ratio to starting numbers \u2013 if Unit had 12 men, it would mean that 4 men are dead because of werewolf. )</li> <li>Now we go to Lunacy phase. Base \u2018Willpower\u2019 dicepool of Unit is 6 ( twice All Other Pools ). From Gauru Form encounter they get -2 penalty. From Primal Urge, Uratha does only -0 penalty. From numbers, Unit get +3 bonus. From attacking them, Unit get +1 bonus. In the end, Unit rolls 8 dices on Lunacy \u2013 rather good dicepool, I must admit.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:15:09-08:00","id":1010126,"title":"","content":"The Lunacy check is not a resisted action. It should only be All Other Pools, not 2*All Other Pools.<br /> <br /> Edit: A resisted action is an action that has a dice pool like this: Attribute + Skill (+ Supernatural Power) - Resistance Attribute<br /> That's when you are supposed to replace Resistance Attribute with All Other Pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-30-2016, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:32:41-08:00","id":1010254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so in this take it would mean that any Gauru sighting in battle ends it instantly in mass Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are still failing to grasp that the Unit is an abstraction. It's not &quot;one soldier fails his roll to resist Lunacy, so the whole squadron falls to Lunacy.&quot; One soldier can't fail the roll because individual soldiers are not making rolls. It's &quot;the Unit failed its roll to resist Lunacy, so some unspecified number of the soldiers fall to Lunacy, and the overall effect on their ability to operate as a team is significant enough to warrant putting a Lunacy Condition on the Unit.&quot; Conversely, if the Unit had succeeded the roll, its likely that an unspecified number of soldiers still fall to Lunacy, but the overall effect on their ability to operate as a team was not enough to warrant putting a Lunacy Condition on the Unit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If one soldier is needed to make mass histeria in Unit, the they base dicepool should be like 2, tops 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>The base dice pool is 3. We already know this because that's how the Nightmare rules work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we add penalties from Form alone and this mean that each battle with werewolves ends in all humans slaughter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, why are you adding penalties from Form and not bonuses from the size of the group? Second of all, even if they fail it's not going to be a slaughter. Lunacy Conditions aren't <i>that</i> bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Without</i> even taking things like morale from fighting enemy ( penalties from Important Characters Down &amp; Dirty ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about Gauru form's Primal Fear ability here, or something from your custom mass combat rules? If it's the former, I wouldn't force Down and Dirty - a whole squadron of Viking warriors shouldn't be considered a lesser foe, even if individual soldiers are. If it's the latter... when your house rules cause the rules as written not to work as intended, the fault isn't with the rulesvas writren, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010075#post1010075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We higher Lunacy dicepool to numbers of 4-6, or this system is without any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's that important to you, just make resisting Lunacy one of the things they're Best At.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-30-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:47:59-08:00","id":1010261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010122#post1010122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's run some test scenario. Assume we have Viking defending Unit vs Viking attacking Uratha commander. Unit just use stats from Horde Brief Nightmare, Uratha commander have starting 2 dots in any Attributes and Skills needed, Primal Urge 1. So we have this situation then...<br /> <br /> Uratha is attacking Unit. He takes Gauru form. He now has Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4 and Weaponry and Brawl Skills at 2 and do +2 Lethal damage from Tooth or Claws.<br /> <br /> In contrast, out Viking Unit would have: Best Dice Pool 7 ( probably Fighting or Swords &amp; Axes, maybe Shield Defense ), Worst Dice Pool 1 and All Other Pools 3. It has Health of 9 and general Defense as 3. Interesting is this quote:</div> </div> </div> </div>As Tessie said, a roll to resist Lunacy is not a resistance Attribute. It's rolled, not applied as a penalty to an attacker's pool, so we don't double All Other in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008677-viking-werewolves-and-mass-combat?p=1010122#post1010122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we <b>should</b> use 2*All Other Pools, as Lunacy roll is Resolve + Composure in normal situations.<br /> <br /> Now, to the proper fight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Uratha declares his Attack Battle Action. He assumes Gauru as Instant action and charg\u00e9 on Vikings Unit. He uses his Claws with his Brawl 2 so he get\u2019s Attack Dicepool 7. Unit is defending themselves \u2013 use Shield Defense of 7. Very equal in here. If Unit would use it normal Defense, it would be 7 vs 3 \u2013 much more in favor of Uratha. For ease of test, let\u2019s assume Uratha get only 1 Success more than Unit. It would be then 3 Lethals for Unit, it is 1/3 of starting Health. ( Number of Damage done to Unit is also casualties ratio to starting numbers \u2013 if Unit had 12 men, it would mean that 4 men are dead because of werewolf. )</li> <li>Now we go to Lunacy phase. Base \u2018Willpower\u2019 dicepool of Unit is 6 ( twice All Other Pools ). From Gauru Form encounter they get -2 penalty. From Primal Urge, Uratha does only -0 penalty. From numbers, Unit get +3 bonus. From attacking them, Unit get +1 bonus. In the end, Unit rolls 8 dices on Lunacy \u2013 rather good dicepool, I must admit.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>If we start with a base dice pool of 3, as per the horror rules, we get 3 from the Horde's All Orher dice pool, +4 for the size of the group (unless this Horse is made up of only 10 or fewer soldiers?), +1 for taking damage from the werewolf, -2 for Gauru form. That's a total of 6 dice. 9 if the Horde spends Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}